   "post_caption": "Alright the day is almost here and ohhhhh man my prediction is that it’s going to be an absolute bloodbath and democrats lose control of both chambers. Sucks that this might be the end of the democratic process we all feel so entitled to…but the good news is that somehow the blame can be thrown at progressives. You know? The ‘unelectable’ left wing of the party who, as a caucus, supported the broadly popular Biden agenda items which ultimately were sunk by moderate third-way triangulators like Joe Manchin and Henry Cuellar.  \n\nThe interesting thing is that it’s still unclear what this election is a referendum on. As much as people predicted this being an election about losing Roe or inflation or (the stupidest narrative in a generation) leaving Afghanistan…somehow, undeniably Donald Trump is still the unifying idea which engulfs the a\nparty and has connective relevance to every position it takes. He’s not going anywhere.\n\nAnd speaking of which, the impact of a Republican house and senate on a 2024 election can not be overstated. But that, is just too dark and unthinkably bad to confront just yet.",
